WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:01.501
Just hours from

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.702
now, Secretary of State

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.471
Tony Blinken will be on his way

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:06.606
to a high stakes visit in Beijing.

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:07.140
The U.S.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.608
leaving the door open

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:09.175
for a face

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:09.909
to face meeting

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:11.778
between Blinken and Chinese President

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:12.979
Xi Jinping.

00:00:12.979 --> 00:00:14.280
Blinken's trip is happening

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.448
in the wake of several

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:17.017
highly charged military

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:18.118
related incidents

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:20.153
between the US and China.

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:21.788
The most recent was earlier

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:23.523
this month in the South China Sea.

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:23.957
You see it

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:25.725
here, a Chinese warship

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:28.261
cutting off a US Navy destroyer.

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:29.029
This is an incident

00:00:29.029 --> 00:00:30.430
that was caught on video

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:32.799
as the Chinese ship came dangerously

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:33.666
close here,

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:35.702
just 150 yards

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:38.104
in front of this American ship.

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:38.671
Today,

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.273
Blinken said that he is prepared for,

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:42.308
quote, candid conversations.

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:45.712
Oren Liebermann is OUTFRONT

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:47.914
A high stakes visit

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:49.816
with low expectations.

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:50.784
Secretary of State

00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:52.452
Antony Blinken heads to China

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:54.287
trying to reopen crucial lines

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:56.523
of communication with Beijing.

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:58.324
Intense competition requires

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:00.093
sustained diplomacy

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:02.328
to ensure that competition does not veer

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:04.931
into confrontation with conflict.

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:07.133
And again, that is what the world expects

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:10.170
of both the United States and China.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.906
Blinken's trip was canceled once before

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:13.540
after the U.S.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.575
shot down a Chinese spy balloon

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:17.110
that flew over sensitive U.S.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:19.112
sites in February.

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:21.448
Since then, relations have declined.

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:23.249
The series of dangerous encounters

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:25.051
between two of the most

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.820
powerful militaries on earth

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.622
ratcheting up the tensions

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:30.657
in late May.

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:31.791
A Chinese fighter jet

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:33.093
sliced in front of a U.S.

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:34.527
reconnaissance aircraft.

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:35.628
An international airspace

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:36.729
over the South China Sea,

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:37.864
according to the U.S.,

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:39.899
forcing the larger, heavier U.S.

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:40.500
plane

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.000
to fly

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.035
through the wake turbulence

00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:43.970
of the Chinese jet.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.506
Days later in the Taiwan Strait,

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:48.007
a Chinese Navy ship

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:50.043
cut 150 yards in front of a U.S.

00:01:50.043 --> 00:01:51.744
destroyer in what the U.S.

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:52.946
called an unsafe

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:54.581
and unprofessional maneuver.

00:01:54.581 --> 00:01:55.982
China said the U.S.

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:57.951
was there for provocation.

00:01:57.951 --> 00:01:58.885
Earlier, Defense

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:00.053
Secretary Lloyd Austin

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:01.020
shared a handshake

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.055
with his Chinese counterpart

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:03.056
in Singapore,

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:04.124
even as Beijing

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:05.592
rejected a formal meeting.

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:07.160
Austin emphasized Friday

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.062
that he's ready for dialog.

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:10.530
The door is open

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.065
and my phone is that

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:14.634
my phone line is open. And so

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:16.336
they can pick up the

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:18.271
phone and call at any time.

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:19.205
A senior White House

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:21.274
official said dialog is how mature,

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:23.209
strong militaries interact

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:24.611
and the stakes are just too high

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:25.745
to avoid these

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:27.514
critical lines of communication.

00:02:27.514 --> 00:02:28.715
But at the highest levels

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:29.782
of the military,

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:30.783
Austin hasn't met

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:33.086
with his Chinese counterpart in a year.

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:34.721
Blinken is now trying to thaw

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:36.389
those frosty relations

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:38.825
as Beijing maintains a deep distrust

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:39.959
about Washington's

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:42.195
intentions for the region and for China.

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:44.264
Mobile Internet and transportation

00:02:44.264 --> 00:02:44.898
The U.S.

00:02:44.898 --> 00:02:47.200
needs to respect China's core concerns,

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:49.035
stop interfering in China's

00:02:49.035 --> 00:02:50.303
internal affairs,

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:52.639
and stop undermining China's sovereignty.

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:55.008
Security and development interests

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:56.776
in the name of competition.

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:57.777
The State Department said

00:02:57.777 --> 00:02:58.912
it's not expecting

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:00.647
a breakthrough from this visit,

00:03:00.647 --> 00:03:02.015
just a realistic approach

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:04.050
to manage the competition of World powers

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:05.818
in a responsible way.

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:08.521
If we want to make sure as we do that

00:03:08.788 --> 00:03:09.789
the competition that we have

00:03:09.789 --> 00:03:12.325
with China doesn't veer into conflict,

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:13.526
the place you start

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:14.460
is with communicating.

00:03:15.929 --> 00:03:16.930
Defense Secretary Lloyd

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:18.865
Austin told lawmakers one month ago

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:21.000
that the US and the Biden administration

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.902
were preparing a weapons drawdown

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:24.504
for Taiwan to ship quickly

00:03:24.504 --> 00:03:25.305
and much the same way

00:03:25.305 --> 00:03:27.373
the US quickly sends weapons to Ukraine.

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:28.708
But we haven't heard

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:29.976
much about it since then

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:32.078
as we await this further announcement.

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:33.646
Brianna, it certainly seems possible

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:35.815
the US has this on hold right now

00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:37.717
so it doesn't disrupt or derail

00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:39.752
this delicate diplomatic process

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:41.454
that Blinken will try to advance here

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:43.823
when he departs in just a few hours.

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:45.391
Oren Liebermann, thank you for that.

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:46.359
OUTFRONT now,

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:47.493
Democratic Congressman

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:49.028
Ro Khanna of California,

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:50.430
who is a member of the House

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:52.532
Oversight and Armed Services Committees,

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:54.968
and also the Select Committee on China.

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:55.902
Sir, thank you so much

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:58.271
for taking the time with us this evening.

00:03:58.271 --> 00:03:59.572
As you see

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:01.507
Secretary Blinken taking this trip,

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:03.643
what do the deliver rebels need to be?

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:04.978
Does he need to meet

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:07.013
with Xi for this trip to be a success?

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:09.415
Brianna, first of all, it's good

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:10.550
that he's going

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:11.951
I would define success

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:12.719
as just

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:15.588
opening the lines of communication.

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:17.257
If we can get military

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:19.559
to military contact back,

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:21.894
if we can have more regular contact

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:23.529
between our secretary of state

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:25.598
and secretary of defense,

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:27.300
I don't think the benchmarks should be

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:30.303
whether he meets GJ ping if that happens.

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:31.804
That's good.

00:04:31.804 --> 00:04:33.006
But the benchmark should be

00:04:33.006 --> 00:04:34.974
how do we get communication

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:37.377
going between our two countries?

00:04:37.377 --> 00:04:39.512
Bill Gates, the billionaire, met

00:04:39.512 --> 00:04:41.481
with Xi today in China.

00:04:41.481 --> 00:04:43.850
She called him a, quote, good friend.

00:04:44.217 --> 00:04:45.285
And it's notable

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:46.886
because this is a visit that comes

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:48.921
just two weeks after Elon Musk

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:50.056
was in China meeting

00:04:50.056 --> 00:04:52.225
with top government officials there.

00:04:52.225 --> 00:04:53.793
Does it concern you

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:54.594
that you have

00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:55.695
people like Gates

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:56.329
and Musk,

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:57.864
these billionaires

00:04:57.864 --> 00:04:59.399
who have a better relationship

00:04:59.399 --> 00:05:01.534
with the Chinese government than U.S.

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:03.403
government? Officials do?

00:05:03.403 --> 00:05:04.837
Brianna, you're absolutely right.

00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:06.873
I mean, you have Bob Iger and Disney, Tim

00:05:06.873 --> 00:05:09.442
Cook at Apple, Elon Musk, Bill Gates,

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:11.210
the NBA commissioner,

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:13.012
who frankly, have more in contact

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:15.081
with China than our own military leaders

00:05:15.315 --> 00:05:16.983
or our own political leaders.

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:19.052
And I believe that's why we

00:05:19.619 --> 00:05:20.286
should applaud

00:05:20.286 --> 00:05:22.121
Secretary Blinken going there

00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:23.356
so that we have that dialog.

00:05:23.356 --> 00:05:24.557
We had dialog

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:25.758
with the Soviet Union

00:05:25.758 --> 00:05:27.460
at the height of the Cold War.

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:28.494
And people should reread

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:29.395
President Kennedy's

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:30.897
speech at American University

00:05:30.897 --> 00:05:31.664
where he said

00:05:31.664 --> 00:05:33.733
we need that dialog even as we seek

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.134
to win the Cold War.

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:36.436
So there are places

00:05:36.436 --> 00:05:38.071
we have to stand up to China,

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:40.640
but that doesn't preclude dialog.

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:41.307
As I mentioned,

00:05:41.307 --> 00:05:42.775
you were on the Armed Services Committee,

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:44.911
so I want to ask you about

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:47.046
Republican Senator Tommy Tuberville,

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:50.149
who is blocking more than 250 nominations

00:05:50.149 --> 00:05:52.185
of generals and admirals

00:05:52.185 --> 00:05:53.653
because of the Pentagon policy

00:05:53.653 --> 00:05:55.455
that provides reimbursement for travel

00:05:55.455 --> 00:05:56.823
and also paid time off

00:05:56.823 --> 00:05:57.957
for service members

00:05:57.957 --> 00:05:59.025
and their family members

00:05:59.025 --> 00:06:00.560
who were stationed in states

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:01.928
where abortion is illegal

00:06:01.928 --> 00:06:03.029
so that they can receive

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:04.230
reproductive care.

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:06.332
I know you think Tuberville is wrong,

00:06:06.332 --> 00:06:06.799
and actually

00:06:06.799 --> 00:06:08.668
Mitch McConnell agrees with you,

00:06:08.668 --> 00:06:09.635
but does Defense

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:12.472
Secretary Lloyd Austin need to engage

00:06:12.739 --> 00:06:15.808
with Tuberville as he is requesting?

00:06:17.443 --> 00:06:17.643
Well,

00:06:17.643 --> 00:06:18.211
we should not

00:06:18.211 --> 00:06:20.480
negotiate with Senator Tupper,

00:06:20.713 --> 00:06:22.949
who has was holding up

00:06:22.949 --> 00:06:24.717
key promotions for his own

00:06:24.717 --> 00:06:25.918
ideological agenda.

00:06:25.918 --> 00:06:27.353
I would never do that.

00:06:27.353 --> 00:06:28.921
Most Democrats wouldn't do that

00:06:28.921 --> 00:06:30.957
just to get our way to hold up

00:06:31.557 --> 00:06:32.592
these promotions.

00:06:32.592 --> 00:06:33.626
And it matters

00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:34.894
because one of the promotions

00:06:34.894 --> 00:06:35.762
being held up

00:06:35.762 --> 00:06:37.663
is our Joint Chiefs of Staff.

00:06:37.663 --> 00:06:39.031
And as you know,

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:40.133
the General Milley

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:42.168
has to retire by October.

00:06:42.168 --> 00:06:43.703
And if the president doesn't

00:06:43.703 --> 00:06:45.705
get his pick in place,

00:06:45.705 --> 00:06:47.607
then we'll have an acting Joint Chiefs

00:06:47.607 --> 00:06:48.040
of Staff.

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:50.109
And that hurts our national security.

00:06:50.309 --> 00:06:52.011
So I just hope that on this

00:06:52.011 --> 00:06:53.679
whatever he other maneuvers

00:06:53.679 --> 00:06:55.448
he wants to do, that's his right.

00:06:55.448 --> 00:06:57.650
But he shouldn't hold up our military.

00:06:58.151 --> 00:07:00.253
Well, it's not held up yet, to be clear.

00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:01.621
But it will be held up

00:07:01.621 --> 00:07:03.790
if he continues to do this.

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:05.224
And I hear you're saying

00:07:05.224 --> 00:07:07.360
not to negotiate with him,

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:09.362
but what other option is there

00:07:09.362 --> 00:07:10.696
as you have Republicans

00:07:10.696 --> 00:07:12.265
like Cornyn, like Senator

00:07:12.265 --> 00:07:13.366
Cornyn, Senator Ernst,

00:07:13.366 --> 00:07:15.001
who are offering him

00:07:15.001 --> 00:07:18.004
these legislative alternatives and he is

00:07:18.004 --> 00:07:19.772
just rebuffing people

00:07:19.772 --> 00:07:21.207
even in his own conference?

00:07:21.207 --> 00:07:22.508
I mean, what else can be done

00:07:22.508 --> 00:07:23.376
at this point?

00:07:23.376 --> 00:07:24.844
Well, I think this is

00:07:24.844 --> 00:07:25.845
for the leadership

00:07:25.845 --> 00:07:27.980
of the Republican caucus to figure out.

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:32.485
I mean, they have responsibly supported

00:07:32.485 --> 00:07:33.853
the armed services.

00:07:33.853 --> 00:07:34.887
We have disagreements.

00:07:34.887 --> 00:07:35.755
But when it comes

00:07:35.755 --> 00:07:37.156
to our national security,

00:07:37.156 --> 00:07:37.924
that when it comes

00:07:37.924 --> 00:07:39.292
to respecting our military,

00:07:39.292 --> 00:07:40.693
that's still fortunately a place

00:07:40.693 --> 00:07:42.462
where there's bipartisan agreement.

00:07:42.462 --> 00:07:42.929
And I

00:07:42.929 --> 00:07:44.730
I hope Senator McConnell and Senator

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:46.199
Cornyn will say there are lines

00:07:46.199 --> 00:07:47.233
you don't cross.

00:07:47.233 --> 00:07:48.167
And one of those lines

00:07:48.167 --> 00:07:49.435
is you don't hamper

00:07:49.435 --> 00:07:51.437
the president from getting the people

00:07:51.437 --> 00:07:53.673
he needs to keep this country safe,

00:07:53.673 --> 00:07:55.508
especially when we have threats in China

00:07:55.508 --> 00:07:57.743
and the threat of Taiwan.

00:07:57.743 --> 00:07:59.512
Congressman, thank you for joining us.

00:07:59.512 --> 00:07:59.912
Thank you.

